INFO:self_evolverec:The new idea for model in iteration 1:
{
  "description": "Add an exactly zero-initialized, bounded scalar recent-history residual to each category's SASRec model. At every causal position, combine unchanged SASRec features with a normalized exponentially weighted pool of recent item embeddings. Omit any added outer normalization so the initial scoring function matches the baseline.",
  "motivation": "The user diagnosis identifies loosely related recommendations and excessive influence from old, occasional interests. Recent evidence provides an observable way to target both failures, although an embedding-similarity residual cannot verify task fit, equipment compatibility, ownership, or unmet need. Electronics' negative tenth-percentile margin motivates examining difficult comparisons. Neither better margins nor the residual itself establishes improved validation HR@10 or temporal-intent modeling.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve baseline loss, sampler, optimizer, backbone normalization, and candidate scoring initially. Use k=5, event-order decay=0.7, and alpha=0.5*tanh(a), with scalar a initialized exactly to zero, as explicitly proposed defaults rather than established optima. Unlike the earlier sigmoid gate, this coefficient permits exact zero and has derivative 0.5 at initialization; it also permits negative values, so describe it as a bounded residual coefficient rather than a probability or guaranteed positive recency preference. Normalize the pooled branch using LayerNorm with the backbone feature dimension and epsilon, initializing scale to one and bias to zero. Do not normalize the combined output again. A nonzero branch permits an immediate coefficient gradient; branch-exclusive parameters initially receive zero gradient. Shared item embeddings still receive backbone gradients. Do not simultaneously zero the branch output. Log the signed coefficient, its gradient, and branch-to-backbone feature norms; there is no expert routing to diagnose.\n\nFor every position t, pool only sequence[max(0,t-k+1):t+1], assigning decay^(t-j) to valid item j and dividing by valid weight sum. Exclude padding, mask final padded features, and never include the target or future interactions. Repeated occurrences contribute repeatedly without implying continuing demand. Preserve the baseline feature and scoring scale. Create the backbone before branch parameters so extra initialization does not consume random numbers ahead of backbone initialization. For matched experiments, restore identical backbone initialization and sampler/RNG state before training; constructing branch parameters can otherwise change later sampling or dropout streams. With dropout disabled, compare initial logits against the untouched baseline on identical prefixes and candidate IDs, requiring agreement within an explicitly logged numerical tolerance such as atol=1e-6 and rtol=1e-5.\n\nPredeclare a budgeted sequence of experiments: untouched baseline; fixed alpha=0.1; learned zero-initialized alpha. Keep k and decay fixed initially. If resources permit, use separate normalization controls: an added outer LayerNorm with residual disabled, and the full residual with outer LayerNorm. For mechanism checks, compare last-item, uniform full-history, uniform recent-window, and exponential recent-window pools while holding embeddings, scoring, loss, and tuning budget constant. Use frozen-model scoring controls to isolate representation effects; separately trained ablations answer a different question. Add training-count popularity and normalized item-kNN controls before attributing gains to temporal intent. Elapsed-time pooling is a later experiment requiring timestamp plumbing in both training and export; use exp(-(t_last_observed-t_j)/tau), never the unknown target timestamp. Shuffle older items while preserving the last item to assess older-context information; permute historical timestamp gaps while preserving item order to assess elapsed-time information. These perturbations are diagnostic hypotheses, not selection metrics or proven causal identification.\n\nPreserve DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, all four category routes, original input splits, single-GPU execution, and the SASREC_EPOCHS environment default of 200. Save architecture configuration, branch parameters, weights, and logs beneath the trial directory. Update the predictor writer to reconstruct exactly the same architecture, padding rules, final-position selection, and scoring path in working/predict.py. Save k, decay, alpha bound, and normalization epsilon. Validate checkpoint reload and candidate-score agreement. No extra datasets, pretrained weights, hidden test access, or evaluator modifications are permitted.\n\nRetain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). The latter must use measured metrics and their definitions. Keep view.model as the actual trained module; view.item_emb references the shared embedding; view.log2feats returns deployed fused features; view.predict_score preserves the existing pairwise and candidate-broadcasting contract. Preserve user_train, meta_data, and review_data interfaces without assuming unavailable fields. Diagnostics consume (None, sequence, positive, negative) batches shaped B x L, exclude padded positions, and use the deployed scoring function. Preserve measured margin definitions and the mapped-cosine embedding statistic; values near 0.5 do not establish severe collapse. Mark unavailable item-category breakdowns explicitly unavailable rather than interpreting empty lists as evidence. Do not invent ratings, review text, item categories, prices, stores, or simulator traits. Keep the native full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for five real training users per category.\n\nPredeclare equal comparison budgets, checkpoint evaluation schedules, and a tie-break rule before results; retain the baseline on exact ties and treat statistically inconclusive selected gains as exploratory. Log every attempted configuration, checkpoint look, failure, and GPU-second cost within the shared 43,200 GPU-second search budget. Select exclusively by unchanged four-category macro validation HR@10 using the pinned 200 users/category, 99 unique negative candidates, and seed 42. If the unchanged evaluator exposes per-user outcomes, cache paired binary hits and bootstrap 200 users with replacement independently within each category for 10,000 CPU replicates, preserving model pairing. Compute delta as the equally weighted mean of category hit-rate differences and report 95% percentile intervals alongside category differences. One changed hit changes category HR by 0.5 percentage points and macro HR by 0.125 points. Intervals condition on fixed checkpoints and candidates, exclude seed/candidate variability, and do not correct winner-selection bias; few discordant outcomes can yield unstable intervals. If per-user outcomes are unavailable, report that limitation without changing the host evaluator.\n\nBuild supplementary next-item diagnostics only from prefixes within training histories. Report counts and differences by category, history length, target training frequency, and repeat versus nonrepeat target. Report whether preprocessing removes repeats; do not change it. Restrict claims of broader temporal benefit unless gains extend beyond short histories and repeat targets and survive similarity/popularity controls. Official validation HR@10 remains the selection criterion, while training-prefix diagnostics explain behavior. Freeze selection before the host's independent held-out evaluation. No user-facing or validation improvement is claimed before measurement.",
  "pseudocode": "class RecentResidualSASRec(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, backbone, dim, eps, k=5, decay=0.7):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.backbone = backbone\n        self.k = k\n        self.decay = decay\n        self.alpha_bound = 0.5\n        self.recent_norm = nn.LayerNorm(dim, eps=eps)\n        self.a = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(()))\n\n    @property\n    def item_emb(self):\n        return self.backbone.item_emb\n\n    def log2feats(self, sequence):\n        # sequence: B x L, right-aligned, zero padded.\n        h = self.backbone.log2feats(sequence)\n        pooled = torch.zeros_like(h)\n        denom = h.new_zeros(sequence.shape + (1,))\n        length = sequence.size(1)\n        for lag in range(min(self.k, length)):\n            # At destination t, source is t-lag; never a future item.\n            source = sequence[:, :length-lag]\n            valid = source.ne(0).unsqueeze(-1)\n            weight = (self.decay ** lag) * valid.to(h.dtype)\n            pooled[:, lag:, :] += self.item_emb(source) * weight\n            denom[:, lag:, :] += weight\n        pooled = pooled / denom.clamp_min(1e-8)\n        r = self.recent_norm(pooled)\n        alpha = self.alpha_bound * torch.tanh(self.a)\n        z = h + alpha * r\n        return z * sequence.ne(0).unsqueeze(-1)\n\n    def score_positions(self, features, items):\n        # Both features and embedded items have shape B x L x D.\n        return (features * self.item_emb(items)).sum(-1)\n\n    def score_candidates(self, final_features, candidates):\n        # final_features: B x D; candidates: B x C.\n        return (final_features.unsqueeze(1) * self.item_emb(candidates)).sum(-1)\n\n# Adapt view.predict_score to its existing broadcasting contract using these scores.\n# Use the unchanged baseline loss and sampling path for training.\n# Export identical construction, causal pooling, and scoring through predictor writer.\n# Verify alpha==0 initialization logits and checkpoint reload scores numerically.\n# Compare the predeclared slate exclusively using pinned macro validation HR@10.",
