  "implementation_notes": "Retain DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, four-category routing, trial-local artifacts, and SASREC_EPOCHS default 200. Preserve the baseline architecture and objective during the initial architectural comparison. No executable baseline files were supplied; the following specifies an implementation rather than claiming a tested replacement.\n\nGraph: construct binary training-only user-item incidence X separately per dataset, C=X.T@X, and degrees d_i=C_ii. Remove diagonal entries. For the primary proposed configuration use S_ij=[C_ij/sqrt(d_i*d_j)]*[C_ij/(C_ij+10)], require C_ij>=3, retain each row’s top 50 neighbors, and keep directed rows after pruning. These are prespecified starting values, not published optima. Compute sparsely without materializing a dense item-item matrix. Compare raw counts, normalized similarities and lift only within a limited declared tuning budget; lift can amplify rare coincidences. Training-only construction excludes held-out interactions, but includes later training events relative to earlier training prefixes. Describe this as an offline graph; strict event-time causality requires time-filtered counts.\n\nRepeated support: for history position t, collect distinct earlier nonpadding item IDs excluding i_t. Set r_t to the mean of S[i_t,i_u] over that set, including zero similarities; use zero for an empty set. Thus r_t lies in [0,1] and depends only on the prefix ending at t. It measures distinct neighboring evidence, not temporal periodicity. Compare this mean with maximum similarity and repeated-support alternatives. Do not add a candidate-level constant R(c) to every history attention logit: softmax cancels it. A candidate graph score could instead be a separately ablated residual, requiring its own scale and popularity controls.\n\nAttention: use the existing hidden dimension and learned bias-free query/key/value projections. For supervised position p, include n