ive_score_k)); for softmax use temperature 1 over one positive and K negatives with no logQ correction for the uniform proposal. Exclude padding, the target and known training positives from sampled negatives, and document replacement behavior for small catalogs. A gBCE arm requires the paper’s exact parameterization and an explicitly logged calibration value before execution. Count diagnostics, graph work charged by the host, failed trials and debugging against the shared budget; report completed updates rather than equating epochs with cost.\n\nEvaluation: use only the pinned four-category macro validation HR@10 for selection, with the same users and candidates across models and a prespecified checkpoint schedule. Report category results and, if the host exposes per-user hits, bootstrap paired users independently within each category and average the four differences for a 95% interval. This is conditional on trained models and fixed candidates and does not correct winner-selection bias. One hit changes category HR by 0.5 percentage points and macro HR by 0.125 points. Worst-case independent-user standard errors are approximately 3.54 and 1.77 points respectively. Popularity/history-length strata are descriptive when accessible without changing the evaluator. Do not interpret sampled HR as full-catalog HR. Log every trial and limit adaptive selection; reserve confirmatory claims for untouched host evaluation.\n\nPredictor and diagnosis: serialize all projections, gates, recency parameters, graph buffers, configuration and item mappings, and update the predictor writer to restore identical scoring and routing. Preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Keep view.model as the trained module. Preserve log2feats(sequence) and predict_score(features, items); retain tensor-shaped features and provide causal context through an explicit model context cache refreshed by log2feats, with correct handling of both final-candidate and BxL diagnostic scoring. Never silently diagnose only the base dot product. Return metrics and metric_definitions measured using the actual combined score and the original diagnostic sampling. Mark category breakdowns unavailable because item categories are unavailable. Use only histories, titles, descriptions and timestamps; never consume review attributes, ratings, prices, stores, hidden test files or pretrained weights. Track simulator mismatch descriptions only when measured, separating unknown specifications from explicit incompatibility. Twenty training users’ qualitative feedback is exploratory and can itself be overfit.",
  "pseudocode": "for each dataset:\n    X = binary_incidence(training_histories)\n    C, degrees = sparse_cooccurrence(X)\n    S = cosine_times_support_shrinkage(C, degrees, tau=10)\n    S = remove_diagonal_filter_support_and_topk(S, min_support=3, k=50)\n    initialize projections normally; a=0; b=0; softplus(ell)=0.1\n\nfor each training batch:\n    h = sasrec(causal_sequences)\n    keys, values = key_projection(h), value_projection(h)\n    for each history position t:\n        U = distinct_nonpadding_items_before(t) minus {item_at(t)}\n        r[t] = mean(S[item_at(t), u] for u in U) if U else 0\n    for chunks of supervised positions p and candidates c:\n        allowed[t] = nonpadding(t) and t <= p\n        logits[t] = dot(query(item_embedding(c)), keys[t]) / sqrt(d)\n        logits[t] -= softplus(ell) * log1p(p-t)\n        logits[t] += tanh(b) * r[t]\n        context = safe_masked_attention(logits, values, allowed)\n        residual = dot(context, item_embedding(c))\n        score[p,c] = dot(h[p], item_embedding(c)) + tanh(a) * residual\n    optimize unchanged_baseline_objective(positive_scores, negative_scores)\n    # Always compute residual in autograd, including when a == 0.\n\nat prespecified checkpoints:\n    evaluate pinned four-category macro validation HR@10\n    record GPU cost, category results, and actual-score diagnostics\nsave selected model, graph, configuration, mappings, and matching predictor writer\n# At inference cache final history projections and chunk candidates.\n# Treat proposed ablations as experiments; do not claim unmeasured gains.",
