# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Only the diagnosis module is supplied; model architecture and sequence-encoder 
internals are unspecified. Diagnosis reads `item_emb.weight`, obtains 
per-position sequence representations through `log2feats(sequence)`, and scores 
positive/negative items with `predict_score(features, items)`. It does not 
explicitly extract a final user representation: margin checks use features at 
all valid sequence positions.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the compatibility view (named `model` in 
this implementation), metadata, review data, and training histories. Reviews and
histories are not used by these probes.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` examines up to ten batches of `(None, 
sequence, positive, negative)`. Sequence inputs are converted to NumPy; positive
and negative tensors are placed on the selected device. Scoring runs without 
gradients after calling `eval()`. With a compatibility wrapper, that call must 
reach the actual `view.model` module.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`:** Samples up to 2,048 non-padding item 
embeddings using seed 42, normalizes them, averages off-diagonal pairwise cosine
similarity, and maps it to `[0,1]`. Higher values indicate greater directional 
alignment; approximately 0.5 means average cosine similarity near zero.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`:** Mean and lower tenth 
percentile of positive-minus-negative logits at positions where the positive ID 
is nonzero. Higher values indicate stronger sampled-pair separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`:** Fraction with negative margin; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`:** Fraction with margin below 0.5; lower 
indicates fewer weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`:** Counts category occurrences 
separately for positive and negative items in weak-margin and incorrect-ranking 
cases.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, input perturbation, gradient analysis, or SVD is 
performed. Random embedding subsampling estimates alignment; loader-supplied 
negatives test pairwise ranking.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The result contains `metrics` and corresponding `metric_definitions`. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis)` embeds both into a prompt 
requesting JSON with `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and 
`evidence`.

These training-batch probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog 
ranking, temporal sensitivity, or user traits. Margins depend on logit scale and
negative sampling. Categories are unavailable in this benchmark, so category 
lists should be empty. Empty valid-position samples produce zero-valued margin 
metrics, which must not be interpreted as evidence of health.

