Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The model implementation is not supplied. Diagnosis uses `item_emb.weight` and 
sequence features returned by `log2feats(sequence)`. It scores positive and 
negative items through `predict_score(features, items)`. Features cover sequence
positions; the probe does not explicitly select or inspect a final user 
representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the compatibility view and its 
`meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is subsequently 
consulted; reviews and stored histories are unused.

The margin probe calls `eval()` on the supplied object, converts sequences to 
NumPy, obtains features, and scores stacked positive/negative IDs shaped `B × L 
× 2`. Positions with positive ID zero are excluded. Scoring runs without 
gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings
using seed 42, normalizes them, and maps their mean off-diagonal cosine 
similarity to `[0,1]`. Higher suggests directional alignment; approximately 0.5 
corresponds to mean cosine zero.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean`:** Average positive-minus-negative score; higher 
indicates stronger separation.
- **`pos_neg_margin_p10`:** Lower-tail margin, highlighting difficult positions;
higher is preferable.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`:** Fraction with negative margin; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`:** Fraction with margin below 0.5; lower 
indicates stronger separation at this score scale.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`:** Counts category occurrences 
separately for positive and negative items in weak-margin and incorrect-ranking 
cases, retaining the top 20 categories.

Margins use at most ten training batches.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, input perturbation, sensitivity testing, SVD, or gradient
analysis occurs. Negative items come directly from the training loader.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both into a prompt requesting JSON 
containing `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`; it 
does not itself generate that interpretation.

Category annotations are unavailable under this task contract, so category lists
will be empty. Training margins do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog 
recommendation quality, or simulator traits. Embedding alignment does not 
directly measure recommendation diversity. Margin thresholds depend on score 
scale, and absent valid positions produce potentially misleading zero defaults.

